FILE: assets/css/touchHandler.css
FEATURE: carousel-verification
DATE: 2026-10-02

================================================================================
CHANGE 1 — touch-action
================================================================================

OLD_SECTION
    .vTouchHandler{
        cursor: grab;
        cursor: -moz-grab;
        cursor: -webkit-grab;
    }
    .vTouchHandler.grab{
        cursor: grabbing;
        cursor: -moz-grabbing;
        cursor: -webkit-grabbing;
    }

NEW_SECTION
    .vTouchHandler{
        cursor: grab;
        cursor: -moz-grab;
        cursor: -webkit-grab;
        /* Hand horizontal drags to the handler and keep vertical page scrolling; without this a phone
           treats a sideways drag as a page gesture and cancels the pointer stream mid-swipe */
        touch-action: pan-y;
    }
    .vTouchHandler.vPanY{
        touch-action: pan-x;
    }
    .vTouchHandler.grab{
        cursor: grabbing;
        cursor: -moz-grabbing;
        cursor: -webkit-grabbing;
    }

REASON
touch-action: pan-y hands horizontal drags to the handler while keeping vertical page scrolling;
.vPanY flips it for a vertical handler. Scoped to .vTouchHandler, which is present only while
touch is enabled, so disableTouch() restores the browser's default. Verified computed
touch-action 'pan-y' and cursor 'grab' on a carousel container.
